-- title:
--   The crossing model W[[u,v]]/(uv-varpi^e) is a normal local domain
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring that is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, let $\varpi \in W$ be irreducible, and let $e$ be a natural number with $1 \le e$. The object under consideration is `UVCrossingModel W (ϖ ^ e)`, by definition the quotient of the ring of formal power series in two variables indexed by `Fin 2` over $W$ by the ideal generated by the single element $X_0 X_1 - C(\varpi^{e})$, where $C$ denotes the constant-coefficient inclusion of $W$; that is, $W[\![u,v]\!]/(uv - \varpi^{e})$. The conclusion is the conjunction of three assertions about this quotient ring: it is an integral domain, it is a local ring, and it is integrally closed in its field of fractions. No regularity is claimed, and indeed for $e > 1$ the ring is not regular.
--
--   This is the normality of the $A_{e-1}$ surface singularity $uv = \varpi^{e}$ over a discrete valuation ring, in the form needed for the local study of a crossing (node) on a modular curve after a possibly ramified base change, where the completed local ring at a node over a ramified coefficient ring is $W[\![u,v]\!]/(uv-\varpi^{e})$ rather than a regular local ring. It is used by the statements about integral closedness of stalks of pullbacks, about units and monomial normal forms in adic completions identified with crossing models, and in the comparison of prolongations at a specialised place.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_isIntegrallyClosed_of_uniformizer_pow.lean

